From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:59:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] ufshci: Auto-Hibernate for a kept link without one

The link kept from the previous kernel gets its Auto-Hibernate timer
back; if that kernel had none, Linux's default: Hibern8 after 150 ms
without requests, left by the controller with the next one, so the link
does not stay active between requests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/dev/ufshci/ufshci_ctrlr.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/dev/ufshci/ufshci_ctrlr.c b/sys/dev/ufshci/ufshci_ctrlr.c
index e536ebbc2..2b1cfa1cf 100644
--- a/sys/dev/ufshci/ufshci_ctrlr.c
+++ b/sys/dev/ufshci/ufshci_ctrlr.c
@@ -398,9 +398,18 @@ ufshci_ctrlr_start(struct ufshci_controller *ctrlr)
 
 	/* TODO: Configure Background Operations */
 
-	/* Hand the kept link its Auto-Hibernate back */
-	if (ctrlr->is_link_kept)
+	/*
+	 * Hand the kept link its Auto-Hibernate back; if the previous kernel
+	 * had none, Linux's default: the link goes to Hibern8 after 150 ms
+	 * without requests (timer scale 3: 1 ms units), and back by itself
+	 * with the next one
+	 */
+	if (ctrlr->is_link_kept) {
+		if (ctrlr->kept_ahit == 0)
+			ctrlr->kept_ahit = 3 << UFSHCI_AHIT_REG_TS_SHIFT | 150;
+		ufshci_printf(ctrlr, "Auto-Hibernate %#x\n", ctrlr->kept_ahit);
 		ufshci_mmio_write_4(ctrlr, ahit, ctrlr->kept_ahit);
+	}
 
 	if (ufshci_sim_attach(ctrlr) != 0) {
 		ufshci_ctrlr_fail(ctrlr, false);
